Which Python packages are required to run this code: ```javascript
// Variables inside a function
function example() {
    let x = 10; // Local variable
    function outer() {
        let y = 20; // Local variable, outside the function
        console.log(x); // Accessing the local variable
        console.log(y);
    }
    outer();
}

// Variables defined globally
let x = 10; // Global variable
function outer() {
    let y = 20; // Local variable, outside the function
    console.log(x); // Accessing the global variable
    console.log(y);
}

example();
```

This will output:

```
10
20
10
20
```

In JavaScript, variables declared inside a function have the same scope as the function itself. This means that if a variable is declared inside a function, it will only be accessible within that function and any functions that call it. 

In contrast, variables declared outside a function have the same scope as the global scope. This means that they can be accessed from anywhere in the program, and can also be accessed from within a function.
